          { name: "Assuming Cultural or Ideological Homogeneity Means Unified Interests", tag: "avoid", why: "At 93.55% white and deeply Republican, it is tempting to assume ME-HD-8 is a culturally monolithic district with unified interests—but the 22% opposition and the 51.4 median age with $48,607 income reveal economic differentiation that cultural similarity masks. Younger adults, rural renters, and fixed-income homeowners have materially different concerns, and a representative who assumes they are all animated by the same political identity rather than serving them around their distinct economic circumstances will find that assumption tested in a more competitive electoral environment." }
