          "Build authentic relationships with Native American constituents and tribal governments in southern Maine; the ~2.7% demographic gap may represent a swing constituency whose turnout and candidate preference are decisive in a 52-48 margin, and whose governance expectations around healthcare access, tribal sovereignty, and economic development require sustained, specific engagement rather than token acknowledgment.",
          "Treat 52% as a contested margin requiring active defense, not a secure majority: any candidate who assumes this district will automatically reelect on inherited partisan loyalty in an aging, economically-stressed, homeowner-dominant community will find that assumption actively disproven by a credible challenger who addresses older voters' concrete concerns with fluency and specificity.",
