          { name: "Neglecting the ~3.68% Demographic Gap as Politically Insignificant", tag: "avoid", why: "While smaller than the demographic gaps in tribal-heavy southeastern Oklahoma districts, the ~3.68% of ME-HD-16's population not captured in the four reported Census categories represents actual people with constituent needs. Whether this gap reflects immigrant communities, multiracial residents, or other populations, treating it as negligible is both a governance failure and a latent electoral vulnerability—a challenger who offers specific constituent attention to these communities can build a wedge into an otherwise consolidated district, particularly if the incumbent has treated them as demographically insignificant rather than as constituents with real service needs." }
