          { name: "Abstract Conservative Positioning Without Constituent Economic Specificity", tag: "avoid", why: "At 20.4% college attainment and $51,336 median income, ME-HD-69 is a working-class and retiree-heavy constituency whose political evaluation is driven primarily by whether government is addressing their material economic concerns—not by abstract ideological positioning. Messaging that relies on conservative rhetorical frames without specific solutions to healthcare costs, property tax burden, and rural service maintenance will be perceived as disconnected from the lived constraints of the district's actual voters and leaves vulnerable voters open to challenger messaging." }
