          { name: "Assuming Educational and Racial Homogeneity Eliminates the Need for Diverse Constituent Engagement", tag: "avoid", why: "At 19.1% college attainment and 94.27% white, the district is demographically narrow, but the 4.3% gap and the college-educated minority still represent constituent groups whose needs exist outside the homeowner-majority narrative. A representative who defaults to serving only the obvious demographic majority and neglects to engage younger adults, college-educated households, and Native American constituents with specific attention is leaving electoral opportunity on the table and governing less than the full community's needs." }
