          "Engage the 34.9% college-educated constituency directly on education funding, workforce development, and the quality of schools—this is the demographic segment most likely to evaluate candidates on substantive policy rather than party label, and the one most vulnerable to a Democratic challenger who articulates a coherent vision for public investment.",
          "Establish visible relationships with the district's institutional anchors: schools, healthcare systems, small-business organizations, and civic institutions that serve the affluent, educated, stable homeowner majority; these relationships generate both constituent goodwill and credibility in the face of future challenge.",
          "Monitor whether future Democratic recruitment and investment attempts to field a credible challenger; unopposed victory in 2024 should trigger vigilance rather than complacency, because the next cycle may reveal whether the current margin is genuinely durable or dependent on the absence of serious opposition."
