          { name: "Defaulting to Partisan Rhetoric Rather Than Governance-Specific Messaging", tag: "avoid", why: "An older, college-educated, property-holding constituency in Maine's professional and managerial class evaluates candidates on concrete governance delivery — education quality, property tax fairness, healthcare access, environmental stewardship — not abstract Republican or Democratic partisan positioning. Generic messaging about 'fiscal discipline' or 'common sense' will underperform in HD-86 relative to issue-specific advocacy grounded in the district's actual governance challenges and constituent priorities. A candidate whose messaging focuses on partisan identity rather than specific answers to education funding, healthcare cost, or property tax burden will struggle to consolidate the 52% against a Democratic opponent who articulates concrete solutions." }
