          "Treat the 48% opposition as information, not noise: in a district this white, this homeowner-heavy, and this educated, 48% Democratic support signals either candidate-specific appeal for the Republican incumbent or genuine issue-driven opposition. Build a campaign that either defends the incumbent's record with specificity or directly addresses the opposition's driving concerns.",
          "Avoid abstract partisan positioning in favor of concrete governance delivery: a college-educated, older, property-holding constituency in Maine evaluates on competence, responsiveness, and whether their specific concerns (education quality, property tax burden, healthcare cost) are being addressed. Generic Republican messaging will underperform in this district relative to issue-specific, governance-focused advocacy."
