          "Build specific engagement with the Black community and communities of color: 23.58% Black, 3% Hispanic, and ~6.6% gap (likely multiracial or other) means communities of color are approaching one-third of the district; criminal justice, economic opportunity, health disparities, and whether state government is delivering for them are the evaluation criteria that determine whether Democratic alignment remains stable or becomes vulnerable.",
          "Address working-class economic pressures directly: the 14.7% college attainment and $48,695 income signal a service-sector and working-class base whose wages have not kept pace with inflation and whose healthcare and childcare costs are rising; wage floors, healthcare expansion, and childcare access are the legislative priorities that translate Democratic alignment into durable constituency relationship.",
          "Do not treat 100% unopposed as a mandate: the absence of opposition reflects a low-salience race in deep blue territory, not strong constituent satisfaction; any candidate who campaigns as though the seat is safe without active engagement risks allowing economic deterioration to erode the Democratic coalition—at which point a well-resourced challenger with sharp messaging on jobs and cost-of-living can surface and create a genuine race."
