          "Engage education quality and funding with specificity: at 43.1% college attainment, this district has substantial stake in K-12 education quality and in whether college pathways and student debt burden are manageable — treat education as a household economic issue, not as an ideological talking point.",
          "Treat 51-49 as a genuinely competitive margin: in an affluent, educated, relatively young suburban district, a one-percentage-point margin is not a hold — it is a signal that college-educated homeowners are actively evaluating both parties on governance competence and fiscal fairness, and any candidate who assumes the existing coalition is locked in will be vulnerable to a credible challenger on those dimensions."
