          { name: "Assuming College-Educated and Renter Constituencies Have Aligned Priorities", tag: "avoid", why: "While both the college-educated professional base (41%) and the renter majority (50.1%) lean Democratic, their policy expectations and economic concerns may diverge significantly. Professionals prioritize education funding and progressive governance; renters prioritize housing affordability and cost-of-living relief. A legislator who assumes these groups are automatically aligned, rather than actively bridging their distinct concerns, risks alienating one or both. Treating them as unified constituencies rather than distinct groups with specific needs is the easiest path to challenger vulnerability." }
