          "Lead on housing affordability and renter protections: at 50.1% renters in a district with $75,464 median income, housing costs are the material economic security issue for half the constituency. Tenant protection legislation, affordable housing development, and rent stabilization are not peripheral—they are the foundation of constituent trust with the largest demographic bloc in the district.",
          "Engage the college-educated professional base on education funding and progressive governance: the 41% college-attainment level and $75,464 income profile skew toward professional-class voters whose policy expectations center on education investment, climate action, and institutional competence. This constituency will defect if they perceive the incumbent as insufficiently committed to these priorities.",
          "Build specific relationships with Black, Asian, and Hispanic communities rather than treating them as a unified minority bloc: at 18.37% Black, 5.39% Asian, and 3.47% Hispanic, these are distinct constituencies with specific economic concerns—workforce development for the Black community, professional advancement and anti-discrimination enforcement for Asian residents, and immigrant-integration and economic mobility for Hispanic families. Representation that treats these communities as interchangeable or secondary to the white professional base creates the vulnerability a challenger can exploit."
