          { name: "Underestimating Turnout Vulnerability", tag: "avoid", why: "A 66% result in a 92.74% white, 66.2% college-educated, $161,389 median-income district reflects strong affiliation rather than high-ceiling persuasion — but it does depend on reliable turnout among a constituency that votes regularly. Any candidate who assumes the district will mobilize automatically or focuses resources on persuasion rather than affirmation and turnout will risk underperforming the baseline and squandering the district's strong Democratic lean." }
