          { name: "Ideological Overreach on Cultural Issues Disconnected from Constituent Material Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "The 65-35 Democratic margin comes from affluent professionals evaluating governance competence, not from strong ideological conviction on cultural or social issues. Any incumbent who pivots away from education, fiscal management, and quality-of-life delivery to emphasize partisan cultural positioning will find the margin compressed and the 35% Republican floor mobilized to contest seats that should be secure. This constituency will support Democratic governance if it delivers on their material concerns; they will defect if they perceive ideology replacing competence." },
          { name: "Taking the 65-35 Margin as Permission to Deprioritize Constituent Service", tag: "avoid", why: "A 65-35 result in a district this affluent and educated is not a mandate for ideological priorities — it is evidence that the incumbent's pragmatic focus on education, fiscal responsibility, and service delivery is resonating. Any incumbent who interprets a 2024 win as permission to reduce engagement, pivot to abstract principles, or assume the base will hold in difficult circumstances is misreading the coalition. This seat is held by active alignment between constituent expectations and incumbent delivery, not by inherited Democratic loyalty. Complacency will compress the margin; specific constituent attention will hold or grow it." }
