          { name: "Economic Mobility & Younger Worker Opportunity", tag: "lean-into", why: "The 31.3 median age combined with 26.3% college attainment and $60,625 median income signals a constituency of younger workers with limited higher education access and constrained wage opportunity in the regional economy. Workforce development, apprenticeship programs, childcare affordability, and support for regional employers who offer above-median wages are the practical policy levers that younger constituents evaluate. An incumbent who speaks specifically to the economic constraints of workers in their twenties and thirties — not abstract prosperity messaging — builds the credibility necessary to hold a constituency that could otherwise organize around economic grievance." },
          { name: "Risks of Unopposed Incumbency & Constituency Erosion", tag: "careful", why: "Running unopposed in 2024 is not a signal of seat durability; it is a signal that opposition has not yet mobilized. In a young, rent-burdened, working-class district where housing costs and wage stagnation are the primary lived experience, unopposed status can create the conditions for reduced constituent engagement and atrophy of visible legislative response to material concerns. If the incumbent approaches the seat with the confidence that 100% margins are stable, or if constituent service capacity erodes during a period of no electoral pressure, a challenger focused on housing and economic mobility could rapidly shift the political geography. The 68.4% renter rate is a structural vulnerability waiting for an opponent to activate it." },
          { name: "Abstract Conservative Messaging Disconnected from Working-Class Economic Reality", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district where renters are 68.4% of households and median income is $60,625, messaging that emphasizes limited government, tax cuts for business, or deregulation as abstract principles will not resonate with younger workers whose material concern is affording rent and building economic stability. If the incumbent or any future representative campaigns on conservative positioning unmoored from specific response to renter hardship or wage stagnation, opposition will rapidly frame this as inattention to the district's actual economic condition." },
          { name: "Assuming Youth Apathy or Lack of Political Organization", tag: "avoid", why: "The 31.3 median age might suggest a constituency that is politically disengaged or difficult to mobilize, but young renter constituencies have demonstrated high capacity for political organization around housing, wages, and cost-of-living issues when candidates speak directly to these concerns. Assuming that younger voters in ME-HD-132 are passive or unlikely to shift their vote based on economic grievance is a strategic error that could allow opposition to build organization unnoticed until it is too late to respond effectively." }
