          "Recognize the demographic vulnerability: a district at 48.2 median age with 19.9% college attainment and $62,038 income is aging in place without clear in-migration or economic growth. The 67% margin is solid, but it depends on holding a shrinking cohort. Long-term seat security requires addressing why younger adults are not choosing to build lives in this district.",
          "Maintain Republican base consolidation through turnout emphasis: with a homogeneous white constituency (94.76%), the 67% margin depends on reliable turnout among older, habitual voters. Any erosion in turnout among this base — whether from burnout, health constraints, or discouragement — directly threatens the margin. Turnout infrastructure and affirmative messaging about why voting matters in a Republican-dominant district are critical.",
