          "Diagnose the 50-50 split as a genuine partisan opening, not a safe seat for either party: a tied result means inherited party loyalty is fractured and persuasion is possible. Any candidate who consolidates only their base and ignores the opposition's driving concerns will hand the seat to whoever can credibly speak to working-class material welfare.",
          "Avoid abstract ideological positioning; every policy argument must connect to direct household economic impact: in a district where college attainment is 33.1%, voters are evaluating candidates on whether they understand their actual problems and can deliver solutions, not on their alignment with partisan orthodoxy.",
