          "Lead on aging homeowner economic security: property tax burden, healthcare cost sustainability, rural hospital viability, and the affordability of aging in place are the material concerns of a 43.8-year-old, 70.5% homeowner constituency at $62,647 income, and they are the issues most likely driving the 50% opposition.",
          "Account for the 4.7% demographic gap: roughly 1,400-1,800 residents are not captured in the four Census categories; in a tied race, understanding who these voters are, where they live, and what their concerns might be (rural communities, younger populations, immigrant households, or other constituencies) is strategically essential rather than a demographic curiosity.",
          "Engage younger adults and renters on economic mobility and housing affordability: the 29.5% renter rate and 31.7% college-educated share represent a constituency evaluating whether Maine offers opportunity; losing this group while relying on older homeowners is a path to losing a 50-50 seat as demographics shift."
