          "Engage education funding and school quality directly — with 30.4% college attainment and a median age of 41.8, many constituents have school-age children or strong community ties to K-12 education; the specific mechanisms by which state policy translates into classroom resources and educational outcomes are concrete, evaluable questions that determine whether this constituency perceives the incumbent as competent.",
          "Articulate a specific vision for municipal service delivery and infrastructure — the 70.2% homeownership rate and $79,895 income indicate constituents with direct stakes in roads, schools, public safety, and water/sewer systems; demonstrate how state policy supports or constrains municipal capacity to deliver these services at the level this community expects and is willing to pay for.",
          "Do not take the 50% as a floor — the opposition's equal share indicates this is a genuinely contested seat where the other half of the constituency made a deliberate choice against the incumbent; assume they did so based on substantive governance disagreement, not partisan activation, and address the specific concerns that made them persuadable."
