          "Lead with housing policy: at 65.3% renter rate in a $71,159-income district, rental market dysfunction, landlord-tenant law, and housing supply are the material concerns of the majority—and the most credible ground for a challenger to win if current constituent needs are unaddressed.",
          "Engage young professionals specifically on economic security: healthcare costs, student loan policy, childcare affordability, and tax burden are the concrete issues that determine whether a highly educated 36.7-year-old renter constituency feels the incumbent is delivering for them or not.",
          "Do not assume partisan loyalty: the 58.9% college education rate in an urban district typically predicts sophisticated, issue-focused voting rather than straight-ticket support; constituents will evaluate on whether their actual economic conditions are improving under current governance."
