          "Engage the affluent homeowner constituency on property tax fairness and municipal service delivery: at $92,877 income with 84% homeownership, property tax burden, school funding adequacy, and infrastructure maintenance are direct household financial concerns that translate to candidate preference — do not assume Republican homeowners are voting Democratic by accident.",
          "Address healthcare access and cost concerns specific to an aging (48.8 median age) affluent constituency: prescription drug pricing, long-term care planning, and Medicare adequacy are material policy concerns for professionals and retirees approaching or in their late career, and specific legislative positions on these issues matter more than partisan framing.",
          "Test whether the Democratic margin reflects genuine policy realignment or sub-performance by the Republican candidate: a 12-point gap in a demographically conservative district is large enough to represent a real shift in voter preference, but also large enough that a stronger candidate or a clear policy agenda on the constituency's actual concerns could materially close it."
